This photo shows a tray after the meal, with only residue left. There is a bowl with a little pink liquid, a bowl with a few bits of food, a plate with orange sauce smears, and a small cup holding some dressing or sauce. The cup has roughly 10 g of liquid at about 4 kcal/g... more precisely, dressing is about 3 kcal/g only if it is oil-based, and this looks thinner, so I'll take about 2 kcal/g, which gives roughly 20 kcal. The plate smears are about 8 g at about 1.5 kcal/g, so about 12 kcal. The bowl with bits is about 8 g at about 1 kcal/g, so about 8 kcal. The pink bowl is about 15 g at about 0.4 kcal/g, so about 6 kcal.

That adds up to about 46 kcal across about 41 g of food.

